      "problem": "$-4\\,+${{field-1}}\n$=0$",
      "worked_solution": "The number that can be added to $-4$ to give $0$ is the additive inverse of $-4.$\n\nTo find the additive inverse of the number $-4$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(-4)=4.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-4)+4=-4+4=0\\,✓\n$$",
